1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,050
Your phone buzzes.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:04,680
Not a bill.

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,090
Not a paycheck.

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:07,580
A share.

5
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:10,937
Your share of the largest fortune ever made.

6
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:13,420
Sounds like a fantasy.

7
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,700
But a few days ago,

8
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,060
one of the companies building

9
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,100
superintelligence promised a piece

10
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,350
of itself to the public good.

11
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:23,300
Then Elon Musk made a promise of his own:

12
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:26,910
a SpaceX share for every child in America.

13
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:29,590
So whose fortune will it be?

14
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:31,020
Let me show you how it could

15
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:33,100
reach every person on Earth.

16
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:33,980
With a plan you could

17
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:36,190
explain to a friend tonight.

18
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,780
The company is Anthropic.

19
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:42,340
It's pledging a slice of itself now.

20
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,300
That slice can climb as its value climbs,

21
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:47,140
if its board agrees.

22
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,580
And Musk added:

23
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:50,900
"This will be the first of many."

24
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:53,670
Both are promises, not contracts.

25
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,900
For now, the pledged shares sit

26
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:58,660
in a fund Anthropic wholly owns.

27
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,300
And the pledge comes just before

28
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,630
the company plans to go public.

29
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,180
But whatever the motives,

30
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:05,460
imagine every company

31
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,380
building this did the same.

32
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:08,740
And imagine your share

33
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,870
grew every time they grew.

34
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,540
Why would any of it be yours?

35
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:15,820
They built it.

36
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:17,950
But look at what they built it from.

37
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,020
So much of what people ever wrote down.

38
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,460
Books and letters.

39
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,140
Songs and research.

40
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,020
Code.

41
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:27,740
A grandmother's recipe, shared online.

42
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,620
A forum answer, written for a stranger.

43
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,860
That's what AI is learning from.

44
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,980
All of us.

45
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,860
So a share of what it makes isn't charity.

46
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,540
It's an inheritance.

47
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:40,620
Thomas Paine put it this way:

48
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,910
"not charity but a right."

49
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,900
And the largest fortune

50
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,260
in history hasn't been made yet.

51
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,937
So it belongs to no one.

52
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:50,900
Yet.

53
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,300
Which means we don't have

54
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,780
to take what anyone already has.

55
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,860
We just have to agree, now,

56
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,670
how to share what's coming.

57
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:02,700
But how do you share a fortune

58
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:04,403
that doesn't exist yet?

59
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,860
There are three ways.

60
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:08,910
The first is to own.

61
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:11,100
Bernie Sanders has a bill.

62
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,260
A tax, paid in new shares,

63
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,620
would hand a public fund

64
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:17,070
half of the big AI companies.

65
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,020
Every year, that fund would pay

66
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:21,420
every American the same dividend.

67
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,020
In polls, roughly two

68
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,260
in three Americans support it.

69
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:27,500
It reaches into the future, too:

70
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,820
shares created later would be taxed as well.

71
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:33,180
Critics expect years in court,

72
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,710
and it stops at the US border.

73
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,920
The second is to print.

74
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,920
Elon Musk wants government

75
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,520
checks for everyone.

76
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,440
He's sure AI will make so

77
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,890
much that prices won't rise.

78
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:49,280
Emad Mostaque, founder of Stability AI,

79
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,200
wants new digital money tied

80
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,330
to every verified human.

81
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,600
The world has done this

82
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:56,480
before, for countries.

83
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,680
A few years ago,

84
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:59,760
the IMF created reserve money

85
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,000
worth hundreds of billions of dollars,

86
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,330
in one go.

87
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,650
It went out by size and wealth.

88
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,290
The poorest countries got a sliver.

89
00:03:09,368 --> 00:03:10,560
If prices hold,

90
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,880
printing takes nothing from anyone.

91
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,520
But nobody ends up owning anything.

92
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,280
And whoever controls the tap

93
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,250
decides who gets what.

94
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,750
The third is to agree.

95
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:23,940
Before the fortune exists,

96
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:26,100
we settle how it will be shared.

97
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,940
Like neighbors agreeing how to split

98
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:30,900
the harvest before the first seed goes in.

99
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:32,580
It's the quietest way,

100
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:34,710
and the one I keep coming back to.

101
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,670
But it has one obvious problem.

102
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,830
You're probably thinking it already.

103
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:43,100
The rich never share.

104
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,780
For what they already own,

105
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:46,910
that doubt is often right.

106
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,050
But this fortune belongs to no one.

107
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,440
Yet.

108
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,080
And where the rules came before the riches,

109
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,840
sharing has worked.

110
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,680
For decades, almost every

111
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,880
Alaskan has received

112
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,440
the same share of the state's oil money.

113
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,760
Every year.

114
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,240
Rich or poor.

115
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,517
Child or adult.

116
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,840
Norway made sure the state owned a share

117
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,680
of its oil before the big money came.

118
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:14,320
Today its fund owns a slice of Nvidia,

119
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,400
a giant of the AI boom.

120
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:19,863
About $11,000 worth for every Norwegian.

121
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,240
Taken as one country,

122
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:25,280
humanity is already almost rich.

123
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,560
Not each of us.

124
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,450
All of us, together.

125
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,480
So here's the plan.

126
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,320
Plant a share for everyone,

127
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,370
now, while it's still small.

128
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,920
Let it grow with every

129
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,680
success of the winners.

130
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,520
Then harvest the same share

131
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,170
for every human being.

132
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,050
Step one: plant.

133
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,090
Right now, these companies are still small.

134
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,960
OpenAI and Anthropic together are worth

135
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,600
about $220 for every person on Earth.

136
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,080
If the fortune comes,

137
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,280
they'll be worth many times that.

138
00:04:58,320 --> 00:05:01,290
So the time to set slices aside is now.

139
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,640
But a share only counts

140
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,400
if it leaves the company.

141
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,360
In our plan,

142
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,560
it goes into an independent fund,

143
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,640
under a fixed rule that no board can change.

144
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,520
That's the difference

145
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,730
between a gift and a right.

146
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:18,460
The first seeds are already in the ground.

147
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,540
The US government turned its subsidies

148
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:23,540
for Intel into a stake in the company.

149
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,860
Before taking office,

150
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,620
South Korea's president floated

151
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,460
a national AI company,

152
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:31,220
partly owned by all its citizens.

153
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:32,860
American babies born these

154
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,140
years can get a thousand

155
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:35,780
government dollars, invested

156
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:37,470
in the stock market.

157
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,900
None of this reaches everyone yet.

158
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,510
It stops at borders, and parents have to

159
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:43,500
apply.

160
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:46,220
But every piece of it can be copied.

161
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:47,980
Picture a girl born tonight,

162
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:49,340
anywhere on Earth.

163
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,260
A seed with her name on it.

164
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,780
By the time she can walk,

165
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:54,430
it's already growing.

166
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,030
Step two:

167
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,340
grow.

168
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,740
Imagine our fund paying every person

169
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:04,070
a fixed slice of its value, every year.

170
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:06,380
Now picture the next headline:

171
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:09,340
"AI company doubles its value."

172
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,820
Today, most of us scroll

173
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:13,140
past and feel left behind.

174
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:16,380
With a share, their win is your raise.

175
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:17,620
Automatically.

176
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,060
Envy turns into something

177
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,710
closer to cheering.

178
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,800
Pieces of this already exist.

179
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,920
The OpenAI Foundation was given

180
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,880
about a quarter of OpenAI,

181
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,600
and gets more if the company's

182
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:31,520
value soars tenfold.

183
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,240
Oxford researchers proposed

184
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,840
a Windfall Clause:

185
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,040
the bigger the profit,

186
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,983
the bigger the share given away.

187
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,680
But who gets to cheer?

188
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,210
Only the people of one rich country?

189
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:45,760
Step three:

190
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:46,960
harvest.

191
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,200
One rule matters most:

192
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,170
the same share for everyone.

193
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,480
Switzerland already does a small version.

194
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,080
Every resident, from baby to pensioner,

195
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,320
gets the same refund

196
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:01,360
from an environmental tax, every year.

197
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,570
It arrives through their health insurance.

198
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,160
Anthropic's plan mentions "direct

199
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,930
distributions to specific populations."

200
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:11,010
But someone would have to pick them.

201
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,730
An equal share needs no one to pick.

202
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,760
No board, no government,

203
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:18,690
no algorithm decides who deserves it.

204
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:21,750
This share wouldn't stop at a border.

205
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:24,790
So far, most plans in the headlines do.

206
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,020
A first step is being negotiated

207
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:28,820
at the United Nations.

208
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,500
Countries could tax digital

209
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,420
services their people use,

210
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,260
AI included, even when

211
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,310
the company sits elsewhere.

212
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:38,710
The United States has left the talks.

213
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:41,940
The accounts already exist.

214
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:44,180
Four in five adults have one,

215
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:45,620
often on their phone.

216
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:49,220
But nobody pays every human on Earth yet.

217
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,300
The pledges depend

218
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:52,420
on boards and billionaires.

219
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:53,980
And there's no global fund

220
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:55,620
to fill those accounts.

221
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:56,580
That's exactly what

222
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,470
we still have to agree on.

223
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,620
So picture the day we do.

224
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:05,390
A care worker in Manila, at dawn.

225
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:08,700
A truck driver in Ohio, at dusk.

226
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:12,220
Two phones buzz at the same moment.

227
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,660
The same share.

228
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:14,940
Not charity.

229
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,510
Their inheritance.

230
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:20,620
That buzz isn't a fantasy.

231
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,990
It's a rule nobody has written yet.

232
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:26,070
It belongs to no one.

233
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,420
Yet.

234
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:32,110
Which means it can still belong to everyone.

235
00:08:33,208 --> 00:08:34,120
We don't have to take

236
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,250
what anyone already has.

237
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:40,470
We just have to agree, now,

238
00:08:41,092 --> 00:08:42,830
how to share what's coming.

